    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1122">

                <pb facs="0810" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/47.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: In thanking you for your
                    note of this day’s date on the subject of the neutralisation of the oil wells, I
                    wish to state that I quite concur in your suggestion to treat the question of
                    the control of the cities independently to that of the oil wells. As you say, it
                    is most important that there should not be delay, for any delay is especially
                    dangerous to the wells. But it is of course of the utmost importance when the
                    time comes that whoever is in control of the towns should clearly understand
                    that proper respect must be paid to the principles of international law and the
                    property of neutrals.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cecil Spring Rice</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
